      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): return empty string for undefined in safeStringify",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`safeStringify` in `src/config/allowed-values.ts` falls through to `String(value)` when `JSON.stringify` returns `undefined`. For `value === undefined`, `String(undefined)` produces the literal string `\"undefined\"`, which is confusing when rendered in the config form UI — a field with no value shows the text `undefined` instead of being blank.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`JSON.stringify(undefined)` returns the value `undefined` (not a string), so the `serialized !== undefined` check skips the early return and the code reaches `String(undefined)` → `\"undefined\"`. Returning `\"\"` for `undefined` is the correct semantic: no value → empty display.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNone in practice — `undefined` values in config are uncommon. This is a defensive fix.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- allowed-values.test.ts: 2/2 pass",
        "branch": "fix/safestringify-undefined-bug",
